{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>If Esav comes to the one camp and strikes it.</b> That is the camp of the maidservants and their children — the camp that is with them — and he strikes them." "<b>And the remaining camp shall escape.</b> That is Leah and Rachel and the camp that is with them. And Scripture explicates the verse fully: ״ויחץ את הילדים על לאה ועל רחל ועל שתי השפחות״. 'Shall escape' — from the sword, in the manner of what is written (Jeremiah 51:50): ״פלטים מחרב״. From here Obadiah learned, who made two groups of the prophets and did not hide them in one place, as it is written (I Kings 18:13): ״ואחביא מנביאי ה׳ וגו׳ חמשים חמשים איש במערה ואכלכלם לחם ומים״. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: a person should always divide his money into thirds — a third in land, a third in merchandise, a third under his hand, as it is said (Deuteronomy 28:8): ״יצו ה׳ אתך את הברכה באסמיך״ — this is merchandise; ״ובכל משלח ידך״ — this is what is under your hand; ״וברכך בארץ״ — this is land." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> 'If Esav comes to the one camp and strikes it' — these are our brethren in the south; 'and the remaining camp shall escape' — these are our brethren in the diaspora. Their intention is to say that our father Jacob knew that the one camp would survive no matter what. And it is a hint for the generations: not all his seed falls into the hands of the children of Esav, nor can they all be consumed throughout the length of their exile, but some will escape against Esav's will. <br><b>And so</b> the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: והיה המחנה הנשאר לפליטה — 'against his will.' And the meaning is that if a king rises and decrees upon us banishment or destruction of life and property in one of the lands, behold, another king in another place will gather and show mercy — and to this the Rabbis, of blessed memory, intended in this Midrash."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:08.024098108Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}